WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
This oval shows everything the camera could see, in every direction, flattened like a map of the world. Straight ahead is the middle.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.950
Below: the time on the camera, and the time for someone watching from far away. Near the black hole, the camera's clock falls behind.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The thin inner circle is light that travelled around the black hole once or more before escaping. The camera is now so fast that the simulation slows down for a better view.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.900
The camera's speed makes everything straight ahead much brighter.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.500
From here, the fall to the event horizon takes the camera ten minutes of its own time.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:48.800
The point of no return. For the distant watcher, the camera never arrives: look at the second clock.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.600
Light from the universe outside still shines in. Nothing can leave.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.300
The camera is destroyed. Microseconds later, it would reach the singularity at the centre.

